## [Troubleshooting](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/troubleshooting.md)

### [Troubleshooting agent installation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-agent-issues.md)

Use this section to troubleshoot issues with installing or running the AWS Replication Agent on your source servers.

- [Agent logs and diagnostics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/agent-diagnostics.md): When troubleshooting Elastic Disaster Recovery agent issues, start by checking the service status and reviewing recent log entries.
- [Agent installation prerequisites](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/agent-install-prerequisites.md): Before installing the AWS Replication Agent, verify that your source server meets the following requirements.
- [Linux installation errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/agent-install-linux-errors.md): Troubleshoot errors encountered during or after AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery agent installation on Linux source servers.
- [Windows installation errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/agent-install-windows-errors.md): Troubleshoot errors encountered during AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery agent installation on Windows source servers.
- [Common agent installation errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/agent-install-common-errors.md): This topic covers platform-agnostic installation errors related to AWS credentials, account configuration, IAM, and agent lifecycle.

### [Troubleshooting replication errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-replication.md)

Use this section to troubleshoot issues with data replication between your source servers and the AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery staging area.

- [Verifying network connectivity](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/verifying-network-connectivity.md): AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery requires two network paths from the staging area for replication to succeed.
- [Agent communication errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/replication-connectivity-errors.md): Troubleshoot replication errors caused by network connectivity issues between the AWS Replication Agent, replication server, and AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery endpoints.
- [Replication infrastructure errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/replication-server-errors.md): This topic covers errors related to the replication server infrastructure, including launching, booting, disk operations, and firewall rules.
- [Replication performance errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/replication-performance-errors.md): This topic covers replication errors related to performance, convergence, and lag in AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery.
- [Agent log messages](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/agent-runtime-errors.md): Troubleshoot replication errors that the AWS Replication Agent writes to its own log on the source server.
- [Bandwidth requirements](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/comm-bandwidth-planning.md): Calculate the required network bandwidth for AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery data replication and measure source server write speed.

### [Troubleshooting launch errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-launch.md)

Use this section to troubleshoot issues that occur when launching drill or recovery instances.

- [Conversion errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/launch-conversion-errors.md): Troubleshoot errors that occur during the conversion phase of launching drill or recovery instances in AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery.
- [Launch configuration errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/launch-configuration-errors.md): Troubleshoot errors caused by launch configuration, permissions, or resource limits in AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery.
- [Windows post-launch issues](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/launch-windows-issues.md): This topic covers Windows-specific issues that can occur after you launch drill or recovery instances with AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery.

### [Troubleshooting failback errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-failback.md)

Use this section to troubleshoot issues that occur during the failback process — from Failback Client setup through reverse replication.

- [Failback Client errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/failback-client-errors.md): Troubleshoot errors encountered during Failback Client setup and connectivity in AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery.
- [Failback replication](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/failback-replication-errors.md): Troubleshoot errors encountered during reverse replication (failback data sync) in AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery.


